course: dictionary
lesson: 2233
title: Cowardly and brave
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cowardly means not brave: too afraid to face danger, pain or something difficult. In The Wizard of Oz, the Cowardly Lion is scared of almost everything, even though he wants to help his friends. Context helps you spot the meaning: a character who runs from a real danger is cowardly.
explain: A cowardly act is different. It is mean and unfair, because the person avoids risk. «Blaming a pet or a baby who cannot answer back is a cowardly lie» shows this: the liar picks someone who cannot defend themselves. Attacking someone weaker, or hiding behind others, is also cowardly.
explain: Be careful, because walking away from a fight is not always cowardly. «When Callum shoved Sam over, Sam stayed down on the floor, didn't fight back, and told a teacher later» is not cowardly, because it stopped the fight growing. Ask yourself: who is at risk, and who is being unfair?
fact: Cowardly means not brave, too afraid to face danger, pain or something difficult.
fact: «A cowardly act» is mean and unfair, because the person avoids risk.
fact: Attacking someone weaker, or hiding behind others, is a cowardly act.
fact: «Cowardly» is an adjective: cowardly, more cowardly, most cowardly.
fact: Walking away from a fight is not cowardly when it stops the fight growing.
exercise: «Letting someone else take your blame is cowardly.» What does cowardly mean here? | *Not brave, and mean and unfair because the person avoids the risk | Very loud and proud | Kind and generous | Quick on your feet
exercise: «Blaming a pet who cannot answer back is a cowardly lie.» Why is this lie called cowardly? | It is a very long lie | It is about the weather | *It picks on someone who cannot defend themselves | It is told by a very brave person
exercise: «Sam stayed down on the floor and didn't fight back.» Was Sam's choice cowardly? | Yes, because he told a teacher | Only if he was crying | *No, because it stopped the fight growing | Always, because he didn't fight
test: Which word means not brave, and too afraid to face danger? | clever | *cowardly | cheerful | curious
test: What does a cowardly attack on a smaller child show? | A funny joke gone wrong | A clever plan | *Mean and unfair, because the attacker avoids risk | Brave and fair play
exam: Which is the best meaning of a cowardly lie? | A true story about a lion | A lie told to make a friend laugh | *A lie told to blame someone who cannot answer back | A brave promise that was kept
